---
description: Writing and content tone for the invitation
alwaysApply: true
---

All copy should sound warm, sincere, and elegant.

Avoid:
- Overly cheesy wording
- Generic romantic clichés
- Corporate language
- Long paragraphs
- Overly youthful slang

Preferred tone:
- “With grateful hearts…”
- “Celebrating 50 years of love, faith, family, and memories…”
- “We invite you to join us…”
- “Your presence would mean so much to our family…”

The site may be bilingual if requested, but do not automatically translate unless asked.

Keep text easy to read for guests of different ages.